Directory: FISSION
File:      actinides_secmin_WMM.readme (24 May 2026)
****************************************************

                         ACTINIDES_SECMIN_WMM.DAT
Properties of secondary-minimum states of selected 75 actinide isotopes with Z=89-98
        (Provided by P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, 24 May 2026)
       *****************************************************************

Contents
--------
The file contains the properties of the secondary minima, including masses, total energies,
macroscopic and microscopic energy contributions, the corresponding deformation parameters,
and excitation energies E* of the secondary minimum relative to the ground state. All calculations
were performed by minimizing the total energy with respect to four mass and axially symmetric
deformation parameters that define the nuclear surface in a standard spherical-harmonic expansion,
while other deformation degrees of freedom were found to be negligible. Further details of the model
and computational procedure can be found in Ref. [1].

Format
------
Each record of the file contains

     Z      : proton (charge) number
     N      : neutron number
     A      : mass number
     M      : ground-state mass excess [MeV]
     Etot   : total ground-state energy [MeV]
     Emac   : macroscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     Emic   : microscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     b2-b8  : deformation parameters at the secondary minimum
     E*     : excitation energy of the secondary minimum relative to the ground state [MeV]

The corresponding Fortran format specification is (3i4,9f8.2).

References
----------
[1] P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 138, 101393 (2021).
